    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0478" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg398"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Cambon</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 443.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In further reply to Mr. de
                    Margerie’s note of the 22d ultimo, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    report of the United States district attorney for the district of Oregon,
                    relative to the violations of the Franco-American consular convention of
                    February 23, 1853, of which complaint was made in the note.</p>
                <p>Hoping that the district attorney’s report will be considered a satisfactory
                    explanation of the matter, I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d352-a1.xml" xpointer="d352-a1"/>
